{"step_index":218,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-19T20:32:02Z","input_tokens":2873,"cache_read_tokens":88014,"output_tokens":514,"content":"Steam installed twice via two different package managers:\n\n1. **Native package (APT):**\n   * Package: `steam-launcher`\n   * Desktop file: `/usr/share/applications/steam.desktop`\n\n2. **Flatpak:**\n   * App ID: `com.valvesoftware.Steam`\n   * Desktop file: `/var/lib/flatpak/exports/share/applications/com.valvesoftware.Steam.desktop`\n\nBoth paths in `XDG_DATA_DIRS`, so Rofi lists both.\n\n---\n\n### How to remove one\n\n**To keep Flatpak, remove Native (APT):**\n```sh\nsudo apt purge steam-launcher steam-libs-amd64\nsudo apt autoremove\n```\n\n**To keep Native, remove Flatpak:**\n```sh\nflatpak uninstall com.valvesoftware.Steam\n```","thinking":"Native Steam and Flatpak Steam are both installed, each with a corresponding desktop entry. The native installation's desktop entry is in `/usr/share/applications/`, while the Flatpak version is at `/var/lib/flatpak/exports/share/applications/`. The Hyprland configuration includes the Flatpak data directory in `XDG_DATA_DIRS`.\n\n\n"}
