{"step_index":249,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-19T20:42:03Z","input_tokens":2349,"cache_read_tokens":95871,"output_tokens":525,"content":"Same reason as Steam. Spotify installed twice via two sources:\n\n1. **Native package (APT):**\n   * Package: `spotify-client`\n   * Desktop file: `/usr/local/share/applications/spotify.desktop`\n\n2. **Flatpak:**\n   * App ID: `com.spotify.Client`\n   * Desktop file: `/var/lib/flatpak/exports/share/applications/com.spotify.Client.desktop`\n\nBoth directories listed in `XDG_DATA_DIRS`, so Rofi shows both.\n\n---\n\n### How to remove one\n\n**To keep Flatpak, remove Native (APT):**\n```sh\nsudo apt purge spotify-client\nsudo rm -f /usr/local/share/applications/spotify.desktop\n```\n\n**To keep Native, remove Flatpak:**\n```sh\nflatpak uninstall com.spotify.Client\n```","thinking":"Spotify is installed twice, indicated by the presence of both native APT and Flatpak versions. This duplication leads to Rofi displaying both entries due to the configuration of `XDG_DATA_DIRS`.\n\n\n"}
